================================================================================
2. disgolink  --  Apache License 2.0
   https://github.com/disgoorg/disgolink
3. disgo      --  Apache License 2.0
   https://github.com/disgoorg/disgo
================================================================================

Both were read as references for how a Lavalink client and a Discord library fit
together in Go: the REST/WebSocket split, the node lifecycle, keeping the wire
types in their own package, and the shape of the voice-state-update callback
gurulink asks for in Config.SendVoiceUpdate. No source file, function body or
type definition was copied from either project. gurulink is distributed under
Apache License 2.0 as well, so nothing these projects require is dropped.


================================================================================
Protocols implemented from public documentation (no code reuse)
================================================================================

  Lavalink v4  --  https://lavalink.dev
    The endpoint paths, gateway ops, event names and JSON field names in
    lavalink/ follow the published v4 protocol. Implementing a documented
    protocol is not reuse of the server's source.

  Kairo, a fork of the Lavalink server
    The extras in lavalink/extras.go target that fork's additions: crossfade,
    tape pitch ramps and next-track pre-buffering. Same situation -- endpoints
    and payloads, no code.


